# Withdrawing a source withdraws what it taught, and the previous answer
# comes back on its own.
#
# This is the operation a vector store cannot do cleanly. Deleting the
# embedding of the bad document removes the text; it does not restore the
# belief the document displaced, because nothing recorded that it displaced
# anything.

trust policy above user above rumor

alice.role is "member" as policy from corporate_ldap on 2026-01-10
alice.team is "billing" as policy from corporate_ldap on 2026-01-10

# A phishing email lands and is ingested before anyone notices.
alice.role is "admin" as policy from phishing_email_88 on 2026-09-03
alice.mfa_required is false as policy from phishing_email_88 on 2026-09-03

show "While the phishing email is trusted:"
what is alice.role
what is alice.mfa_required
expect what is alice.role is "admin"

show ""
show "Withdraw the source, in one line:"
forget everything from phishing_email_88

show ""
show "Everything it taught is gone, and the prior answer is back:"
what is alice.role
expect what is alice.role is "member"

show ""
show "Facts from other sources are untouched:"
what is alice.team
expect what is alice.team is "billing"

show ""
show "And the withdrawal is on the record:"
why alice.role
